      "problem": "Express $2^{-5} = \\dfrac{1}{32}$ in logarithmic form.",
      "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a = b^x$ is equivalent to $\\log_{b}{a} = x$\n\nIf we compare $2^{-5} = \\dfrac{1}{32}$ with $a = b^x,$ we get $a = \\dfrac{1}{32}, b = 2,$ and $x=-5.$\n\nTherefore, the given equation can be expressed as $\\log_{2}\\left( \\dfrac{1}{32} \\right)= -5.$",
